  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1233 PM MDT Mon Jun 8 2026\n\nA trough digging into the Great Basin continues sending some\nweak moisture across the region. A dry slot has intruded on this\nfeature today. But, a broad cumulus field has still taken hold\non most terrain across the West Slope. ATmospheric dynamics on\nthe morning sounding here at Grand Junction are really not in\nfavor of the convective environment we saw yesterday. However, a\nfew showers could reach the surface in trace amounts. The\nboundary layer remains too dry, hence the widespread critical\nfire weather conditions we continue to produce.\n\nThe trough sends a strong jet streak across the region Tuesday.\nThis will send surface winds up into 20-30 mph range across the\nregion, with gusts to around 50 mph. Wind Advisories were \nissued for some valleys in addition to Red Flag Warnings. Gusty\nwinds will amplify the critical fire conditions Tuesday,\nespecially where single digit relative humidity remains in\nplace. The trough settling south Tuesday will introduce some\nweak moisture for our northern counties late in the afternoon,\nwhich will help some with fire weather. This will include some\nchances for another shower or thunderstorm.\n\nThe deepest portion of the trough will work through late Tuesday\nnight. However, broad cyclonic flow will remain stretched over\nthe region, with strong winds aloft continuing. This could\nproduce another day of strong winds for northeast UT and\nnorthwest CO on Wednesday. Red Flag Warnings continue on\nWednesday for much of the region. Winds diminish on Thursday,\nbut Fire Watches have been issued for some areas west of the \nDivide. This trend likely continues into the weekend, as\ntemperatures surge in excess of 10 degrees over normal again.\nThis hot and dry pattern will produce areas of critical fire \nweather again. Models are hinting at some return moisture\nworking northward beneath the high Friday and beyond. Whether\nthis yields any shower activity over the weekend, remains a low\nconfidence forecast. It is looking likely that we remain hot and\ndry for much of the region, hoping for a few clouds and a shower\nto chip away at the heat a bit.",
